{"id":"000W7B","title":"DisequilibriSum","author":"Major314","solvedCount":2,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-24T02:16:37+00:00","posted":"Gestern, 22:41 Uhr","rules":"This puzzle was made in response to the recent Dorlir prompt, encouraging setters to make more chaos construction puzzles featuring 4 regions instead of 6. Enjoy !\n\nChaos Construction : Divide the grid into four non-overlapping regions of orthogonally connected cells. Fill each region with the digits 1-9 such that no digit repeats in any row, column, or region.\n\nUneven Region Sum Lines : Region borders divide blue lines into non-overlapping segments with equal sums. Different lines may or may not have different sums. Additionally, blue lines must follow the two following rules :\n\n• No two segments on a line have the same length.\n• A line of length X contains at least once the digit X.\n\nKropki dots :\nDigits separated by a yellow Kropki dot are non-consecutive.\nDigits separated by a gray Kropki dot are either consecutive or in a 1:2 ratio (i.e one is two times the other).\n\nTry it on SudokuPad","solutionCode":"Row 3 from left to right, with a \"-\" for region borders (eg. 123-456)","tags":["Sudoku","Irregular (Variante)","Region Sum Lines (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/kaggh06rlw","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/kaggh06rlw","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":6,"cols":6,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-24T02:16:37+00:00"}